# Cloudflare Pages routing rules. Existing static files are served first; these
# only apply when no file matches the request.
#
# A request for a missing /assets/ chunk must return a real 404 - NOT the SPA
# fallback (index.html, HTTP 200). Serving 200-HTML for a .js URL is what lets
# a browser cache the wrong body as the chunk's content and then fail every
# dynamic import until a hard refresh. A 404 is never stored as the module, so
# the vite:preloadError reload below can recover cleanly.
/assets/*  /index.html  404

# Everything else is the single-page app: serve index.html so client routing
# (react-router) can take over.
/*  /index.html  200
